# trivy allowlist for ONE image: agent-novnc-signin (deploy/images/novnc-signin).
#
# ci.yml's `trivy (agent-novnc-signin)` job reads this file on top of
# .trivyignore (TRIVY_IGNORES); no other scan reads it, so an id here silences
# nothing in any other image. The RULES in .trivyignore apply: every id names
# the package, why it does not reach us, and the date and who accepted it.

# xwayland 2:24.1.6-1 (agent-novnc-signin only). xwayland present only as
# cage's hard Depends; the /usr/bin/Xwayland binary is removed at build and
# asserted absent by the image gate; no fixed version in Debian.
# Accepted 2026-10-20 by the overseer for 0.10.0. Reviewed and renewed 2026-11-19
# by the owner: Debian still lists both as will_not_fix and the binary is still
# removed and asserted absent. Next review date 2026-12-19: each id carries
# trivy's exp: so it lapses then and the scan fails until someone reviews it.
# Delete both when Debian 13 ships a fix.
CVE-2026-34000 exp:2026-12-19
CVE-2026-34002 exp:2026-12-19

# FFmpeg 7:7.1.5-0+deb13u1 (agent-novnc-signin only): libavcodec61,
# libavfilter10, libavformat61, libavutil59, libpostproc58, libswresample5 and
# libswscale8, pulled in by chromium. The flaw is a heap write in the deband
# filter's runtime command; chromium decodes media through FFmpeg but builds no
# filter graph, so nothing in the image runs that filter. Debian lists it as
# fix_deferred. Accepted 2026-11-24 by the owner for 0.10.5 and 0.11.0-rc.2.
# Next review date 2026-12-24: the id carries trivy's exp: so it lapses then and
# the scan fails until someone reviews it. Delete it when Debian 13 ships a fix.
CVE-2026-135736 exp:2026-12-24
